1
00:00:35,455 --> 00:00:38,982
[ Horns Blowing ]

2
00:02:47,954 --> 00:02:51,685
Sita, go and tell Sister Clodagh
I wish to speak to her.

3
00:02:53,125 --> 00:02:58,085
Therefore, X is equal to 5...

4
00:03:01,200 --> 00:03:06,103
- or minus--
- Reverend Mother wishes
to speak to you, Sister Clodagh.

5
00:03:06,172 --> 00:03:08,106
Joya.

6
00:03:16,148 --> 00:03:18,639
Continue the lesson.

7
00:03:34,600 --> 00:03:36,898
Sister Clodagh,

8
00:03:36,969 --> 00:03:40,530
we may proceed
with our plans at Mopu.

9
00:03:40,606 --> 00:03:44,167
- It will be called Saint Faith.
- Saint Faith.

10
00:03:44,243 --> 00:03:47,735
And you have been appointed
to take charge of St. Faith.

11
00:03:47,813 --> 00:03:51,010
- l, Reverend Mother ?
- You.

12
00:03:51,083 --> 00:03:55,019
You will be the youngest
sister superior in our order.

13
00:03:59,725 --> 00:04:01,818
Thank you, Reverend Mother.

14
00:04:04,030 --> 00:04:07,522
The agent at Mopu
is an Englishman.

15
00:04:07,600 --> 00:04:10,068
He seems a difficult man.

16
00:04:10,136 --> 00:04:12,969
You won't get
much help from him.

17
00:04:15,041 --> 00:04:18,101
[ Man's Voice ]
Dear Madam, My name is Dean.

18
00:04:18,177 --> 00:04:20,737
I am the agent
of General Toda Rai at Mopu...

19
00:04:20,813 --> 00:04:23,680
and I am writing to you
in that capacity.

20
00:04:23,749 --> 00:04:26,877
I understand the general has offered you
the old palace at Mopu...

21
00:04:26,953 --> 00:04:29,820
to make a school and
a dispensary for the natives.

22
00:04:29,889 --> 00:04:32,858
It's not the first time
he's had such ideas.

23
00:04:32,925 --> 00:04:36,486
He's asked me to tell you
about the place and the people.

24
00:04:36,562 --> 00:04:40,589
It's not a comfortable spot,
and it's at the back of beyond.

25
00:04:40,666 --> 00:04:42,827
First you have to get
to Darjeeling,

26
00:04:42,902 --> 00:04:46,394
then I have to find you ponies
and porters to take you into the hills.

27
00:04:46,472 --> 00:04:48,940
Mopu is 8,000 feet up.

28
00:04:49,008 --> 00:04:52,273
The peaks on the range opposite
are nearly as high as Everest.

29
00:04:52,345 --> 00:04:55,280
The people call the highest peak
Nanga Dalle.

30
00:04:55,348 --> 00:04:58,249
It means "the bare goddess. "

31
00:04:59,719 --> 00:05:01,949
I live down in the valley,
out of the wind.

32
00:05:02,021 --> 00:05:04,455
So does the general,
and so do the people.

33
00:05:04,523 --> 00:05:08,391
Mopu Palace stands in the wind
on a shelf on the mountain.

34
00:05:08,461 --> 00:05:12,022
It was built by the general's
father, to keep his women there.

35
00:05:12,098 --> 00:05:15,363
It's called a palace, but there
may be a slight difference...

36
00:05:15,434 --> 00:05:17,994
between your idea of a palace
and the general's.

37
00:05:18,070 --> 00:05:20,300
Anyhow, there it is.

38
00:05:20,373 --> 00:05:24,400
The people are like mountain peasants
everywhere-- simple, independent.

39
00:05:24,477 --> 00:05:27,810
They work because they must,
they smile when they feel like it...

40
00:05:27,880 --> 00:05:31,247
and they're no respecters
of persons.

41
00:05:31,317 --> 00:05:34,650
The men are men-- no better,
no worse than anywhere else.

42
00:05:34,720 --> 00:05:37,655
The women are women.
The children, children.

43
00:05:37,723 --> 00:05:41,022
Up on the mountain above the
palace, we have our holy man...

44
00:05:41,093 --> 00:05:43,721
who sits there day in
and day out in all weathers.

45
00:05:43,796 --> 00:05:47,095
All the people around
are very proud of him...

46
00:05:47,166 --> 00:05:49,464
and bring him food
and little offerings.

47
00:05:49,535 --> 00:05:52,868
The wind up at the palace
blows seven days a week,

48
00:05:52,938 --> 00:05:56,169
so if you must come,
bring some warm things with you.

49
00:05:56,242 --> 00:05:59,507
Nobody has lived there for
a long time, except Angu Ayah...

50
00:05:59,578 --> 00:06:02,411
who's always been there
and stays on as caretaker.

51
00:06:02,481 --> 00:06:05,143
As a caretaker,
she's a bit of a failure,

52
00:06:05,217 --> 00:06:09,119
but she's a faithful, dirty old
bird and goes with the place.

53
00:06:09,188 --> 00:06:11,952
She lives there alone...

54
00:06:12,024 --> 00:06:14,322
with the ghosts of bygone days.

55
00:06:18,931 --> 00:06:22,594
[ Voices Echoing ]
Ayah ! Ayah ! Ayah ! Ayah !

56
00:06:22,668 --> 00:06:26,434
Ayah ! Ayah ! Ayah !

57
00:06:26,505 --> 00:06:30,441
Ayah ! Ayah ! Ayah !

58
00:06:38,751 --> 00:06:43,279
[ Choir Singing ]

59
00:07:31,403 --> 00:07:33,496
Ayah ! Ayah !

60
00:07:33,572 --> 00:07:35,506
Ayah !

61
00:07:48,354 --> 00:07:51,653
[ Indistinct Shouting ]

62
00:08:00,366 --> 00:08:03,767
[ Shouting Continues ]

63
00:08:26,959 --> 00:08:29,894
[ Chattering ]

64
00:08:47,313 --> 00:08:49,907
Ayah ! Ayah !

65
00:08:49,982 --> 00:08:54,214
- [ Ayah ] That's Mr. Dean.
- Never mind Mr. Dean. He'll find us.

66
00:08:54,286 --> 00:08:58,586
Now listen, Ayah.
I have invited some ladies...

67
00:08:58,657 --> 00:09:01,387
to stay here
at the house of women.

68
00:09:01,460 --> 00:09:06,363
Ladies ! Oh, that will be
like old times !

69
00:09:06,432 --> 00:09:08,730
It will not be in the least
like old times.

70
00:09:08,801 --> 00:09:10,928
They are not
that kind of lady at all.

71
00:09:11,003 --> 00:09:14,404
- Then they won't be any fun.
- They are not coming for fun.

72
00:09:14,473 --> 00:09:18,705
These are nuns.
Do you know what a nun is?

73
00:09:18,777 --> 00:09:21,712
They kneel and pray all day like
the monks you invited last year.

74
00:09:21,780 --> 00:09:26,149
I'm going to give them this house
to make a school and a hospital
for the people.

75
00:09:26,218 --> 00:09:29,153
You know nobody here
wants a school...

76
00:09:29,221 --> 00:09:31,553
and I'm sure they
don't want a hospital !

77
00:09:31,624 --> 00:09:35,025
[ Toda Rai ]
How do they know what they want
until they try ?

78
00:09:35,094 --> 00:09:38,120
The people have
all kinds of diseases.

79
00:09:38,197 --> 00:09:41,132
- They have ringworm.
- They don't mind having ringworm.

80
00:09:41,200 --> 00:09:43,964
Then they ought to mind.
And it will all be free.

81
00:09:44,036 --> 00:09:47,335
It was free last time,
and nobody came.

82
00:09:47,406 --> 00:09:50,000
They will this time.
Mr. Dean !

83
00:09:50,075 --> 00:09:52,669
You will receive them for me,

84
00:09:52,745 --> 00:09:55,805
and you will do everything for them
that they want doing.

85
00:09:55,881 --> 00:09:58,873
You too. You will
engage servants for them,

86
00:09:58,951 --> 00:10:02,318
and you will both look after them until
they care to look after themselves.

87
00:10:02,388 --> 00:10:05,619
What do they eat?
How do I know what nuns eat?

88
00:10:05,691 --> 00:10:08,023
I have remembered that.

89
00:10:11,430 --> 00:10:13,557
Do you see that crate?

90
00:10:13,632 --> 00:10:16,567
[ Chattering Continues ]

91
00:10:18,170 --> 00:10:22,072
Sausages.
They will eat sausages.

92
00:10:22,141 --> 00:10:24,837
Europeans eat sausages
wherever they go.

93
00:10:24,910 --> 00:10:29,370
They will eat them when they
come and until they can cook
what else they want to eat.

94
00:10:29,448 --> 00:10:31,780
[ Chattering ]

95
00:10:33,452 --> 00:10:36,148
Now remember, Ayah,
if you give any trouble,

96
00:10:36,221 --> 00:10:38,280
you will be sorry.

97
00:10:38,357 --> 00:10:40,848
I'm sorry now !

98
00:11:03,315 --> 00:11:06,944
A convent in this house.
What do you think of that?

99
00:11:08,320 --> 00:11:11,346
The brothers only stayed
five months.

100
00:11:11,423 --> 00:11:14,290
Perhaps the sisters
won't stay long, either.

101
00:11:19,031 --> 00:11:23,968
[ Reverend Mother ]
The house is 9,000 feet up--
very cold, but good air.

102
00:11:24,036 --> 00:11:29,099
General Toda Rai, who has invited us
to Mopu, has promised us every help.

103
00:11:29,174 --> 00:11:32,109
He was a little afraid
when he learned...

104
00:11:32,177 --> 00:11:35,544
that we are bound to our order
only by yearly vows.

105
00:11:35,614 --> 00:11:38,447
- I explained this rule to him.
- Yes, Reverend Mother.

106
00:11:38,517 --> 00:11:41,816
For more than a century,
to serve voluntarily...

107
00:11:41,887 --> 00:11:44,412
has been one of the glories
of our order.

108
00:11:44,490 --> 00:11:46,685
And our greatest strength.

109
00:11:46,759 --> 00:11:50,718
Exactly.
He understands now.

110
00:11:50,796 --> 00:11:54,288
- Is there anything
you would like to ask?
- Who am I to take with me?

111
00:12:04,610 --> 00:12:08,102
Remember, a community
is not a class of girls.

112
00:12:08,180 --> 00:12:12,139
The sisters won't be easy
to manage or to impress.

113
00:12:14,153 --> 00:12:16,121
Now, let me see.

114
00:12:21,260 --> 00:12:25,458
I'll give you Sister Briony.
You'll need her strength.

115
00:12:25,531 --> 00:12:27,692
Thank you, Reverend Mother.

116
00:12:31,036 --> 00:12:34,028
Sister Philippa for the garden.

117
00:12:36,408 --> 00:12:38,433
- Sister Blanche.
- Sister Blanche?

118
00:12:38,510 --> 00:12:41,377
- You know what the others call her ?
- Sister Honey.

119
00:12:41,447 --> 00:12:44,314
Yes, Honey. I think
you'll need Sister Honey.

120
00:12:44,383 --> 00:12:46,681
She's popular,
and you'll need to be popular.

121
00:12:46,752 --> 00:12:49,243
[ Nuns Giggling ]

122
00:12:55,427 --> 00:12:58,055
- And Sister Ruth.
- But Sister Ruth is ill.

123
00:12:58,130 --> 00:13:00,860
That is why I want her to go.

124
00:13:03,335 --> 00:13:05,667
Forgive me for saying so,
Reverend Mother,

125
00:13:05,737 --> 00:13:09,571
but do you think our
vocation is her vocation?

126
00:13:11,343 --> 00:13:14,141
Yes, she's a problem.

127
00:13:14,213 --> 00:13:17,774
I'm afraid she'll be
a problem for you too.

128
00:13:17,850 --> 00:13:20,910
With a smaller community,
she may be better.

129
00:13:20,986 --> 00:13:25,889
Give her responsibility, Sister.
She badly wants importance.

130
00:13:25,958 --> 00:13:28,859
Do you think it's a good thing
to let her feel important?

131
00:13:28,927 --> 00:13:34,365
Spare her some of your own
importance... if you can.

132
00:13:34,433 --> 00:13:38,563
Mother, are you sorry that I have been
appointed to take charge of St. Faith?

133
00:13:38,637 --> 00:13:42,198
Yes. I don't think
you're ready for it,

134
00:13:42,274 --> 00:13:44,765
and I think you'll be lonely.

135
00:13:48,780 --> 00:13:51,510
Never forget,
we're an order of workers.

136
00:13:51,583 --> 00:13:55,075
Work them hard.
And remember...

137
00:13:55,154 --> 00:13:58,521
the superior of all
is the servant of all.

138
00:13:58,590 --> 00:14:00,581
I understand.

139
00:14:30,322 --> 00:14:33,257
[ Bell Clanging ]

140
00:14:35,994 --> 00:14:39,020
- [ Chattering ]
- It was a good, good idea.

141
00:14:39,097 --> 00:14:41,429
[ Chattering Continues ]

142
00:14:41,500 --> 00:14:44,401
One thing about them,
they keep good time.

143
00:14:46,538 --> 00:14:50,440
- Go !
- [ Murmuring ]

144
00:14:50,509 --> 00:14:53,444
[ Bell Continues ]

145
00:14:56,648 --> 00:14:59,617
[ Horns Blowing ]

146
00:15:33,552 --> 00:15:36,487
[ Chanting ]

147
00:15:50,802 --> 00:15:53,965
[ Sister Philippa ]
Dear ! The whole garden's
so terribly overgrown,

148
00:15:54,039 --> 00:15:56,269
I don't know where to begin !

149
00:15:58,243 --> 00:16:01,337
Please come and help the fat
lady who has questions.

150
00:16:01,413 --> 00:16:04,473
Sister Briony?
Ayah, you must learn our proper names.

151
00:16:04,549 --> 00:16:06,642
Anyway, there aren't
any patients yet.

152
00:16:06,718 --> 00:16:09,050
Oh, aren't there?
There are dozens waiting.

153
00:16:09,121 --> 00:16:11,055
And more coming every minute.

154
00:16:11,123 --> 00:16:15,059
[ Shouting, Chattering ]

155
00:16:20,332 --> 00:16:23,426
[ Crowd Sighs ]

156
00:16:23,502 --> 00:16:26,630
[ Chattering Continues ]

157
00:16:26,705 --> 00:16:31,074
Now tell them to go away and come
and help me with the ones that are left.

158
00:16:31,143 --> 00:16:34,203
[ Sister Clodagh ]
Oh, Sister Blanche, these girls
are to work in your lay school.

159
00:16:34,279 --> 00:16:36,213
They were sent by the general.

160
00:16:36,281 --> 00:16:38,306
Oh, don't they look nice.

161
00:16:38,383 --> 00:16:40,476
But, Sister, you
ought to see the children.

162
00:16:40,552 --> 00:16:42,543
The schoolroom's
full of them already.

163
00:16:42,621 --> 00:16:44,555
The little ones are so sweet.

164
00:16:44,623 --> 00:16:46,648
Some of them can scarcely
do more than toddle.

165
00:16:46,725 --> 00:16:48,920
Joseph Anthony has come.

166
00:16:48,994 --> 00:16:51,428
Ayah, you must knock
before you come in.

167
00:16:51,496 --> 00:16:54,056
- Who is Joseph Anthony?
- Who is Joseph Anthony?

168
00:16:54,132 --> 00:16:57,260
He's the son of the general's cook.
He's going to interpret for you.

169
00:16:57,336 --> 00:17:00,328
He speaks English.
Come in.

170
00:17:06,978 --> 00:17:09,503
- Has the general sent you?
- Yes, lady.

171
00:17:09,581 --> 00:17:11,845
She isn't a lady.
She's a sister.

172
00:17:11,917 --> 00:17:13,851
Say, "Yes, Lemani. "

173
00:17:13,919 --> 00:17:17,252
Yes, Lemani. I have my books
and my bedding outside.

174
00:17:17,322 --> 00:17:20,587
- I shall live here with you.
- Oh !

175
00:17:20,659 --> 00:17:23,457
Would you like to see
my books and my bedding, lady?

176
00:17:23,528 --> 00:17:27,259
Sister ? Lemani?
[ Speaking Hindi ]

177
00:17:27,332 --> 00:17:30,426
- How old are you?
- Six to eleven.

178
00:17:30,502 --> 00:17:32,527
What did you say?

179
00:17:32,604 --> 00:17:34,663
I can remember that I'm six,

180
00:17:34,740 --> 00:17:37,903
but my father married
my mother 11 years ago...

181
00:17:37,976 --> 00:17:40,536
so that I may probably
be about ten.

182
00:17:42,180 --> 00:17:45,115
Sister, the schoolroom
is overflowing with children.

183
00:17:45,183 --> 00:17:47,117
We've nothing unpacked yet.

184
00:17:47,185 --> 00:17:50,177
No one understands the language.
There are too many of them,
and they smell.

185
00:17:50,255 --> 00:17:53,782
- I don't know what to do.
- Why don't you tell them
to come back later ?

186
00:17:53,859 --> 00:17:57,226
- Start with the older ones.
- They won't go away.

187
00:17:57,295 --> 00:18:01,026
- Oh, why not?
- They were paid to come,
so they can't go away.

188
00:18:01,099 --> 00:18:03,465
- Paid?
- [ KnockAt Door ]

189
00:18:03,535 --> 00:18:07,369
Sister, the general's clerk
has orders to pay everybody
who comes to my dispensary.

190
00:18:07,439 --> 00:18:11,341
- So they all want to come.
- Excuse me, Sister, may I suggest?

191
00:18:11,410 --> 00:18:14,675
- Yes, Sister ?
- Wouldn't it be a pity
to send the children away?

192
00:18:14,746 --> 00:18:18,238
- They were paid to come.
- But if they like it,
they may come again.

193
00:18:18,316 --> 00:18:21,251
What can you do with them?
They look very stupid to me.

194
00:18:21,319 --> 00:18:23,879
Remember, they can't speak
a word of Hindustani or English.

195
00:18:23,955 --> 00:18:26,753
Joseph can.

196
00:18:26,825 --> 00:18:29,988
You'll help us,
won't you, Joseph?

197
00:18:30,061 --> 00:18:32,495
The brothers left
a blackboard in the school.

198
00:18:32,564 --> 00:18:34,828
I'll draw things on it
in colored chalk.

199
00:18:34,900 --> 00:18:38,700
They can tell me their name for it,
and I'll tell them the English.

200
00:18:38,770 --> 00:18:41,330
I can take their names and ages
and make a register.

201
00:18:41,406 --> 00:18:43,431
You can hardly
call that a lesson.

202
00:18:43,508 --> 00:18:46,306
You can call it
a very sensible idea.

203
00:18:46,378 --> 00:18:48,369
Thank you, Sister Blanche.

204
00:18:56,755 --> 00:19:00,088
[ Men Shouting ]

205
00:19:13,772 --> 00:19:16,206
I suppose you know who I am.

206
00:19:16,274 --> 00:19:18,469
You must be Mr. Dean.

207
00:19:22,147 --> 00:19:24,081
I must.

208
00:19:24,149 --> 00:19:28,210
And you must be
the sister superior.

209
00:19:33,625 --> 00:19:36,992
What curious feathers. Are they all
from the birds that you've shot?

210
00:19:37,062 --> 00:19:39,428
I don't shoot birds.

211
00:19:41,132 --> 00:19:44,260
When you've shot everything,
it appalls, doesn't it?

212
00:19:46,571 --> 00:19:49,039
I'm the general's agent.
He welcomes you to Mopu.

213
00:19:49,107 --> 00:19:51,041
Understood you wanted to see me.

214
00:19:51,109 --> 00:19:53,270
We want to talk to you on business.

215
00:19:53,345 --> 00:19:56,178
I didn't suppose you wanted
to talk to me on anything else.

216
00:20:00,485 --> 00:20:03,147
Sorry.
Perhaps that wasn't fair.

217
00:20:03,221 --> 00:20:06,816
Mr. Dean, you know
that General Toda Rai...

218
00:20:06,892 --> 00:20:10,191
has given us this house for
a new foundation of our order.

219
00:20:10,262 --> 00:20:12,196
We very much appreciate it.

220
00:20:12,264 --> 00:20:14,892
It's very generous of him.

221
00:20:14,966 --> 00:20:18,959
Yes. You'd like
the general, Sister.

222
00:20:19,037 --> 00:20:22,564
- He also has a superior being.
- Really !

223
00:20:24,309 --> 00:20:27,073
I don't know why you are being
so rude to me, Mr. Dean.

224
00:20:27,145 --> 00:20:29,875
I have to talk business with you
whether I like it or not.

225
00:20:29,948 --> 00:20:33,816
Well, talk it then,
and don't teach at me.

226
00:20:35,720 --> 00:20:38,245
It's no place to put a nunnery,
I can tell you that.

227
00:20:38,323 --> 00:20:41,520
Difficult, but not impossible.
Nothing is impossible--

228
00:20:41,593 --> 00:20:43,857
Is yours a contemplative order ?

229
00:20:43,929 --> 00:20:47,763
I mean, do you live in meditation?
Do you keep solitude?

230
00:20:49,334 --> 00:20:52,895
Our order isn't in the least like that.
We're very busy people.

231
00:20:52,971 --> 00:20:55,030
We're going to open
a dispensary,

232
00:20:55,106 --> 00:20:57,074
a school for children
and a class for girls.

233
00:20:57,142 --> 00:21:01,943
Good. You'll be doing me
a great favor when you begin
to educate the local girls.

234
00:21:06,151 --> 00:21:09,951
I have already been told, Mr. Dean,
that you do not believe in solitude.

235
00:21:13,058 --> 00:21:15,925
Do you know what the people
call this place?

236
00:21:15,994 --> 00:21:17,985
"The House of Women. "

237
00:21:18,063 --> 00:21:20,896
The general's father
used to keep his ladies here.

238
00:21:20,966 --> 00:21:24,094
From now on, it will be known
as the House of St. Faith.

239
00:21:24,169 --> 00:21:27,297
Sister, will you have
that picture taken down?

240
00:21:33,912 --> 00:21:36,437
I give you
till the rains break.

241
00:21:38,149 --> 00:21:41,084
[ Drumming ]

242
00:22:09,047 --> 00:22:12,414
[ Drums Continue In Distance ]

243
00:22:12,484 --> 00:22:15,920
Oh, dear, dear.

244
00:22:15,987 --> 00:22:18,547
[ Knocking At Door ]

245
00:22:18,623 --> 00:22:20,853
Who is it?

246
00:22:20,925 --> 00:22:23,052
Sister Briony.

247
00:22:34,172 --> 00:22:36,231
I can't sleep.

248
00:22:42,047 --> 00:22:44,242
Anything wrong, Sister ?

249
00:22:44,315 --> 00:22:47,443
It's Sister Ruth.
I've just seen her.

250
00:22:47,519 --> 00:22:49,953
- How is she?
- She's sick.

251
00:22:50,021 --> 00:22:53,787
She has violent pains in her joints,
a boil on her finger...

252
00:22:53,858 --> 00:22:55,792
and headaches.

253
00:22:55,860 --> 00:22:57,953
It's this wind.

254
00:22:58,029 --> 00:23:00,054
And they all seem so tired.

255
00:23:00,131 --> 00:23:02,065
It's the altitude.

256
00:23:04,769 --> 00:23:07,533
Our dispensary
is more crowded than ever.

257
00:23:07,605 --> 00:23:12,269
This big house to look after
and all the unpacking still to be done.

258
00:23:12,343 --> 00:23:15,107
And the plumbing's
broken down again.

259
00:23:15,180 --> 00:23:18,115
What do you think, Sister ?
Perhaps Mr. Dean--

260
00:23:18,183 --> 00:23:20,947
Certainly not.
We can manage without Mr. Dean.

261
00:23:21,019 --> 00:23:23,010
Yes, of course.

262
00:23:28,493 --> 00:23:31,428
- Are you all right, Sister ?
- Of course I'm all right.

263
00:23:31,496 --> 00:23:34,522
- Show me your arm.
- I'm perfectly all right.

264
00:23:38,369 --> 00:23:40,633
- So you've got them too.
- What have I got?

265
00:23:40,705 --> 00:23:44,266
Spots. I've got them.
Every one of us has got them.

266
00:23:44,342 --> 00:23:47,368
There must be something
in the water here that's very unhealthy.

267
00:23:47,445 --> 00:23:50,642
- The natives drink it.
- They get sick themselves.

268
00:23:50,715 --> 00:23:54,207
I ask as the general's heir,
the young general.

269
00:23:54,285 --> 00:23:56,219
He's very ill.

270
00:23:56,287 --> 00:23:59,347
[ Drums Continue ]

271
00:23:59,424 --> 00:24:02,359
Those drums
are beating for him.

272
00:24:02,427 --> 00:24:05,658
The beat all night
while he's ill.

273
00:24:08,433 --> 00:24:11,197
If you hear them stop,
he's dead.

274
00:24:26,885 --> 00:24:29,319
[ Drums Stop ]

275
00:24:33,725 --> 00:24:36,592
[ Chattering ]

276
00:25:01,152 --> 00:25:03,086
You !

277
00:25:03,154 --> 00:25:05,213
How do you do?

278
00:25:05,290 --> 00:25:07,884
What are you doing here?

279
00:25:07,959 --> 00:25:10,860
Skew's all filthy.
I have to have it taken off.

280
00:25:10,929 --> 00:25:13,727
I've come to mend
a loose joint in your pipe.

281
00:25:13,798 --> 00:25:16,733
- You must send a plumber.
- The nearest one's Darjeeling.

282
00:25:16,801 --> 00:25:19,201
- I count plumbing among my other gifts.
- That's not the point--

283
00:25:19,270 --> 00:25:23,138
I swear to you, Sister,
it's only the pipe I'm interested in.

284
00:25:23,208 --> 00:25:26,143
- I must see Sister Clodagh about this.
- All right.

285
00:25:26,211 --> 00:25:29,237
I forbid you to stay in there.

286
00:25:29,314 --> 00:25:31,248
All right.

287
00:25:39,490 --> 00:25:43,392
We have to build a workroom
and a school and, later on, a chapel.

288
00:25:43,461 --> 00:25:46,828
Somebody's got to put locks on my
cupboards. I daren't unpack a thing.

289
00:25:46,898 --> 00:25:51,062
And the windows don't open and the door
won't shut and the plumbing won't work.

290
00:25:54,839 --> 00:25:58,070
- Come in, Mr. Dean.
- May I go now, Sister ?

291
00:26:01,713 --> 00:26:04,181
Please sit down, Mr. Dean.

292
00:26:08,419 --> 00:26:11,217
- Would you like some coffee?
- Can you make it decently?

293
00:26:11,289 --> 00:26:15,089
- Can I make coffee !
- Can she?

294
00:26:15,159 --> 00:26:17,650
Full of grits.

295
00:26:19,864 --> 00:26:22,094
Mr. Dean, Joseph tells us...

296
00:26:22,166 --> 00:26:24,191
the people are still
being paid to come to us.

297
00:26:24,269 --> 00:26:28,467
Ah, the general's a wise man.
It's only till it becomes habit.

298
00:26:28,539 --> 00:26:30,973
Let it become a habit
for them to come,

299
00:26:31,042 --> 00:26:33,476
and they won't remember
a time when they didn't.

300
00:26:33,544 --> 00:26:36,172
Then gradually
he'll leave off paying them.

301
00:26:36,247 --> 00:26:39,478
and gradually it'll become
a habit with 'em not to be paid.

302
00:26:39,550 --> 00:26:43,748
- They're like children.
- He told me he was going
to order them to come.

303
00:26:43,821 --> 00:26:47,689
- They don't know what an order is.
- They should learn.

304
00:26:47,759 --> 00:26:51,559
- Why ?
- We all need discipline.

305
00:26:51,629 --> 00:26:54,427
Without discipline, we should
all behave like children.

306
00:26:54,499 --> 00:26:58,367
- Don't you like children?
- [ Door Opens ]

307
00:27:02,907 --> 00:27:05,375
Thanks, Sister Briony.

308
00:27:16,220 --> 00:27:18,654
[ Sighs ]

309
00:27:21,926 --> 00:27:24,156
Talking of medicine,
Sister Briony,

310
00:27:24,228 --> 00:27:26,196
if you get a bad case,

311
00:27:26,264 --> 00:27:30,701
one that seems as though
it might be dangerous, don't take it.

312
00:27:30,768 --> 00:27:32,998
- But that would be--
- It would be wise.

313
00:27:33,071 --> 00:27:36,040
If you got a bad case and
some of your people died,

314
00:27:36,107 --> 00:27:38,439
you'd have all the people
up against you.

315
00:27:38,509 --> 00:27:41,637
- Why ?
- Well, you must remember,
they're primitive people...

316
00:27:41,713 --> 00:27:43,943
and like, like children.

317
00:27:44,015 --> 00:27:46,381
Unreasonable children.

318
00:27:46,451 --> 00:27:50,148
They've never seen medicine. They'd
think it was magic, a new kind of magic.

319
00:27:50,221 --> 00:27:53,019
So remember,
I've warned you.

320
00:27:53,091 --> 00:27:56,151
By the way, how are you
feeling, all of you?

321
00:27:56,227 --> 00:27:59,094
Not very well.
Sister Ruth is the worst.

322
00:27:59,163 --> 00:28:02,064
I think the water must be bad.
Ayah says it's the water.

323
00:28:02,133 --> 00:28:04,601
On the contrary.
The water's too good.

324
00:28:04,669 --> 00:28:08,161
It's Darjeeling tummy.
I'd better get that plumbing fixed.

325
00:28:08,239 --> 00:28:09,968
Sister Clodagh !

326
00:28:11,709 --> 00:28:13,904
What has happened, Sister ?

327
00:28:13,978 --> 00:28:16,640
Oh, Sister, Sister,
they brought in a woman.

328
00:28:16,714 --> 00:28:19,376
Our first bad case.
She was covered in blood.

329
00:28:19,450 --> 00:28:21,975
I've never seen such a sight.
She must've cut an artery.

330
00:28:22,053 --> 00:28:25,454
I had such a time stopping
the bleeding. I've never seen
bleeding like that before.

331
00:28:25,523 --> 00:28:28,822
I didn't know what to do at first,
but at last I managed to stop it.

332
00:28:28,893 --> 00:28:32,260
A minute would've fetched Sister Briony
who would've stopped it at once.

333
00:28:32,330 --> 00:28:34,958
What were you doing there?
I told you to stay in bed.

334
00:28:35,033 --> 00:28:37,467
I was only trying
to consider you, Sister Briony.

335
00:28:37,535 --> 00:28:40,868
It might have been better
to have considered the woman
who is bleeding to death.

336
00:28:45,443 --> 00:28:48,378
- Shall I wait?
- We are coming in a moment.

337
00:28:48,446 --> 00:28:50,914
I think you'd better
go back to your room.

338
00:28:59,490 --> 00:29:02,584
Good-bye, Sister.
I hope your patient does well.

339
00:29:02,660 --> 00:29:04,594
Who is she?

340
00:29:04,662 --> 00:29:07,825
It sounded like "Samuel,"
but it couldn't be, could it?

341
00:29:07,899 --> 00:29:10,299
Oh, Samil.
She's a good old soul.

342
00:29:10,368 --> 00:29:13,895
One of my best workers.
I'm very much obliged to you.

343
00:29:13,971 --> 00:29:15,768
Thank you.

344
00:29:29,320 --> 00:29:32,050
[ Sisters Gasp ]

345
00:29:39,597 --> 00:29:42,566
Now the old place
is a proper convent.

346
00:30:11,262 --> 00:30:13,628
Hello, Sister Ruth.
Going for a walk?

347
00:30:13,698 --> 00:30:15,689
It's time to ring the bell.

348
00:30:15,766 --> 00:30:17,700
You're slipping.

349
00:30:19,170 --> 00:30:21,832
Quarter of an hour early.

350
00:30:27,678 --> 00:30:29,612
Thank you.

351
00:30:36,020 --> 00:30:39,012
I came to ask Mr. Dean
to wait in the blue room.

352
00:30:39,090 --> 00:30:41,149
How did you know he was here?

353
00:30:41,225 --> 00:30:43,352
I saw him from the schoolroom.

354
00:30:45,696 --> 00:30:48,529
I've brought something for you.

355
00:31:01,646 --> 00:31:05,047
Her name is Hersempul,
but we call her Kanchi.

356
00:31:05,116 --> 00:31:09,018
She's 17, she's an orphan...

357
00:31:09,086 --> 00:31:12,385
and it's high time
she was married.

358
00:31:12,456 --> 00:31:16,017
Every evening when I come home,
I find her sitting on my veranda.

359
00:31:16,093 --> 00:31:19,187
She dresses herself up,
puts flowers in her hair.

360
00:31:19,263 --> 00:31:21,857
It's becoming
an absolute nuisance.

361
00:31:21,933 --> 00:31:25,334
If she's cloistered for a few months,
her uncle will marry her off.

362
00:31:25,403 --> 00:31:28,736
But she's been behaving
so badly that no one wants her.

363
00:31:28,806 --> 00:31:31,331
I don't think we want her, either.

364
00:31:31,409 --> 00:31:34,071
Why did you bring her to us?

365
00:31:34,145 --> 00:31:36,943
Isn't it your business
to save souls?

366
00:31:37,014 --> 00:31:39,983
You are not to speak to me
like that, Mr. Dean.

367
00:31:40,051 --> 00:31:41,985
Sorry.

368
00:31:42,053 --> 00:31:45,113
Can't she go into
some sort of service?

369
00:31:45,189 --> 00:31:48,317
She'd set any house by the ears.

370
00:31:48,392 --> 00:31:51,725
I thought no one would have patience
with her, except you.

371
00:31:56,734 --> 00:31:59,828
Would you ask Sister Briony
to come here, please?

372
00:32:03,140 --> 00:32:05,574
[ Whistles ]
Kanchi.

373
00:32:19,724 --> 00:32:23,091
Kanchi.
[ Speaking Hindi ]

374
00:32:59,163 --> 00:33:02,462
Are you sure there's no question
you're dying to ask me?

375
00:33:05,136 --> 00:33:07,070
None.

376
00:33:11,642 --> 00:33:13,576
You wanted me, Sister ?

377
00:33:13,644 --> 00:33:16,306
I have agreed to have this
girl with us for a while.

378
00:33:16,380 --> 00:33:19,213
Can you find somewhere
for her to sleep?

379
00:33:19,283 --> 00:33:23,151
- What is she to do?
- Sister Honey can take her
into the lay school.

380
00:33:23,220 --> 00:33:25,279
Yes.

381
00:33:25,356 --> 00:33:27,790
Tell Ayah to give her
some housework, keep her busy.

382
00:33:32,530 --> 00:33:34,464
Come along.

383
00:33:53,651 --> 00:33:55,585
Well, thanks.

384
00:33:55,653 --> 00:33:59,111
I've heard about the young general's
death. Is the general grieving?

385
00:33:59,190 --> 00:34:01,283
Can never tell with these people.

386
00:34:01,359 --> 00:34:03,919
- What's the new young general's name?
- Dilib Rai.

387
00:34:03,994 --> 00:34:07,259
He was going to Cambridge, but now
he'll be a warrior and marry young.

388
00:34:07,331 --> 00:34:10,027
It'll suit him, all right.
These Rashpits are a fighting race.

389
00:34:10,101 --> 00:34:12,262
Cannon.

390
00:34:12,336 --> 00:34:14,827
[ Together ]
Cannon.

391
00:34:14,905 --> 00:34:16,998
Warship.

392
00:34:17,074 --> 00:34:19,838
Warship.

393
00:34:19,910 --> 00:34:23,175
- Bayonet.
- Bayonet.

394
00:34:23,247 --> 00:34:25,841
Dagger.

395
00:34:25,916 --> 00:34:27,349
Dagger.

396
00:34:40,097 --> 00:34:42,497
- Gun.
- Gun.

397
00:34:44,602 --> 00:34:48,470
You know, Nina, we may have to mix
something with it.

398
00:34:48,539 --> 00:34:50,803
Here, let me have a look.

399
00:35:07,124 --> 00:35:09,991
[ Bell Clanging ]

400
00:35:26,043 --> 00:35:29,342
Hail Mary, full of grace,
blessed is the fruit--

401
00:35:29,413 --> 00:35:32,644
[ Bell Continues ]

402
00:35:53,270 --> 00:35:55,204
Sister.

403
00:35:55,272 --> 00:35:57,900
Did you hear the bell ?

404
00:36:03,614 --> 00:36:07,880
This morning in chapel, I suddenly
had the feeling you were not with us.

405
00:36:07,952 --> 00:36:10,546
- I try hard enough.
- Try what?

406
00:36:10,621 --> 00:36:13,954
I used to forget
everything in chapel.

407
00:36:14,024 --> 00:36:17,289
I used to feel light
and happy and near God.

408
00:36:17,361 --> 00:36:20,990
Let me help you.
What is worrying you?

409
00:36:21,065 --> 00:36:24,762
I remember things
before I joined our order.

410
00:36:24,835 --> 00:36:27,235
Things I wanted to forget.

411
00:36:27,304 --> 00:36:30,603
I never thought of them
until now.

412
00:36:30,674 --> 00:36:33,734
I've been 2 1 years in the order,

413
00:36:33,811 --> 00:36:36,245
and now they come back to me.

414
00:36:37,982 --> 00:36:40,746
I think you can see too far.

415
00:36:40,818 --> 00:36:46,085
I look out there, and then
I can't see the potato I'm planting.

416
00:36:46,156 --> 00:36:51,321
And after a bit, it doesn't seem
to matter whether I plant it or not.

417
00:36:53,497 --> 00:36:58,298
It's this place with its strange
atmosphere and new people.

418
00:36:58,369 --> 00:37:02,271
Stay with me tonight after chapel,
and we will pray together.

419
00:37:02,339 --> 00:37:04,534
And work, Sister.
Work hard.

420
00:37:04,608 --> 00:37:07,702
Work until you're too tired
to think of anything else.

421
00:37:36,040 --> 00:37:39,134
[ Woman's Voice ]
Oh, isn't it a grand day ?

422
00:37:53,557 --> 00:37:56,025
Isn't it a grand day?

423
00:37:56,093 --> 00:37:58,027
Mmm.

424
00:38:05,736 --> 00:38:07,670
What's wrong, Con?

425
00:38:07,738 --> 00:38:09,729
- Everything.
- What specially?

426
00:38:09,807 --> 00:38:13,106
Oh, nothing.
You wouldn't understand.

427
00:38:14,511 --> 00:38:16,445
Is it money?

428
00:38:17,715 --> 00:38:19,706
Whatever else is it?

429
00:38:19,783 --> 00:38:22,217
Desmond's with
a lot of it in Michigan.

430
00:38:22,286 --> 00:38:24,516
I heard from him last week.

431
00:38:26,090 --> 00:38:28,024
He's been made a partner.

432
00:38:28,092 --> 00:38:31,357
And just because I'm the eldest son,
I have to stay here in Ireland...

433
00:38:31,428 --> 00:38:34,261
and hang around
waiting for... this.

434
00:38:37,501 --> 00:38:42,598
[ Sighs ]
I'll have a little money
when I marry, Con.

435
00:38:42,673 --> 00:38:44,800
It isn't a little money.
It's a fortune.

436
00:38:44,875 --> 00:38:48,367
Then it would be a waste.

437
00:38:48,445 --> 00:38:52,006
Clo, don't you sometimes
itch to get away?

438
00:38:52,082 --> 00:38:55,518
No, I don't want to go away.

439
00:38:55,586 --> 00:38:59,579
I want to stay here like this
for the rest of my life.

440
00:39:05,195 --> 00:39:08,130
[ Dog Whimpering ]

441
00:39:08,198 --> 00:39:11,531
[ Dog Barking ]

442
00:39:11,602 --> 00:39:14,594
[ Dogs Barking ]

443
00:39:57,214 --> 00:39:59,808
[ Barking Continues ]

444
00:40:03,253 --> 00:40:05,687
[ Dog Barking ]

445
00:40:10,294 --> 00:40:13,786
[ Man Shouting ]
Ayah ! Angu Ayah !

446
00:40:16,500 --> 00:40:18,434
[ Shouts ]

447
00:40:44,928 --> 00:40:47,829
Ayah ! Angu Ayah !

448
00:40:51,735 --> 00:40:54,602
Salom, my little general.

449
00:40:54,671 --> 00:40:57,504
I want to see
the reverend sisters.

450
00:41:04,248 --> 00:41:06,239
Why are they called
the servants of Mary?

451
00:41:06,316 --> 00:41:09,149
Is the superior sister
called Mary?

452
00:41:09,219 --> 00:41:11,983
Ask her.
Here she comes.

453
00:41:12,055 --> 00:41:14,751
Go now.
I will speak to her alone.

454
00:41:23,934 --> 00:41:26,698
- Good morning.
- Good morning.

455
00:41:26,770 --> 00:41:30,638
- I want to see the superior sister.
- I am the sister superior.

456
00:41:30,707 --> 00:41:34,404
Oh. I want to be
a student here with you.

457
00:41:34,478 --> 00:41:36,673
I want to study
a lot of learning.

458
00:41:36,747 --> 00:41:39,841
I want to study mathematics,
history, poetry and languages.

459
00:41:39,917 --> 00:41:43,216
I have a note from my uncle
to ask you to encourage me.

460
00:41:43,287 --> 00:41:46,882
I'm very sorry.
We only teach children and young girls.

461
00:41:46,957 --> 00:41:50,051
- Why?
- Convents don't teach men pupils.

462
00:41:50,127 --> 00:41:52,061
That's not very polite to men.

463
00:41:52,129 --> 00:41:55,121
We don't mean it that way.
It's the custom.

464
00:41:55,199 --> 00:41:57,667
Convents are for girls.
The brotherhoods are for men.

465
00:42:01,238 --> 00:42:03,399
Jesus Christ was a man.

466
00:42:05,742 --> 00:42:07,835
He took the shape of a man.

467
00:42:07,911 --> 00:42:10,880
But you don't need
to count me as a man.

468
00:42:10,948 --> 00:42:13,917
I'm only interested
in studious things.

469
00:42:13,984 --> 00:42:17,420
Please, Sister. I've written out
my timetable. May I read it to you?

470
00:42:17,487 --> 00:42:20,820
"5:00 a.m. to 7:00 a.m.,
algebra with the mathematical sister.

471
00:42:20,891 --> 00:42:25,089
"8.:00 a.m. to 10.:00 a.m.,
religion, Christianity
with the scriptural sister.

472
00:42:25,162 --> 00:42:27,096
" 10.:00 a.m., art.

473
00:42:27,164 --> 00:42:31,100
" 1:00 p.m. to 3:00 p.m.,
French and Russian with the French
and Russian sisters, if any.

474
00:42:31,168 --> 00:42:34,535
3:00 p.m. to 4:00 p.m.,
physics with the physical sister."

475
00:42:41,144 --> 00:42:43,704
[ Man Shouts ]

476
00:43:36,733 --> 00:43:39,827
[ Door Opens ]

477
00:43:39,903 --> 00:43:42,838
[ Sister Clodagh ]
Please wait in here, General.

478
00:44:27,951 --> 00:44:31,387
Aren't you afraid with
the young general that you've
let a cuckoo into your nest?

479
00:44:31,455 --> 00:44:34,618
If he didn't want to offend the general,
he might turn us out?

480
00:44:34,691 --> 00:44:37,057
[ Chuckles ]
Oh, he wouldn't do that?

481
00:44:37,127 --> 00:44:39,960
You may have trouble
with Kanchi.

482
00:44:40,030 --> 00:44:44,057
- Kanchi ? She'd never dare.
-[ Monks Chanting ]

483
00:44:44,134 --> 00:44:49,071
After all, he is a prince,
and she is what she is.

484
00:44:49,139 --> 00:44:52,575
Still, I expect she knows the story
of the prince and the beggar maid.

485
00:44:52,642 --> 00:44:55,338
We're at 40, 4 1, 42,

486
00:44:55,412 --> 00:44:59,371
43, 44, 45, 46,

487
00:44:59,449 --> 00:45:02,907
47, 48, 49--

488
00:45:02,986 --> 00:45:05,079
When the general
gave us the deeds,

489
00:45:05,155 --> 00:45:07,749
our boundary line was to be
500 yards around the building.

490
00:45:07,824 --> 00:45:09,587
Right.

491
00:45:09,659 --> 00:45:13,254
- So the holy man
is living on our ground.
- He was here first.

492
00:45:13,330 --> 00:45:17,096
Yes, but, Mr. Dean, I find
all these things very distracting.

493
00:45:17,167 --> 00:45:19,863
- Distracting?
- Yes, disturbing.

494
00:45:19,936 --> 00:45:23,929
This clear air,
and the wind always blowing.

495
00:45:24,007 --> 00:45:27,943
And the mountain, and the holy man
sitting there day in, day out.

496
00:45:28,011 --> 00:45:30,104
And the people
coming to see him.

497
00:45:30,180 --> 00:45:32,273
They climb the path
by the house,

498
00:45:32,349 --> 00:45:34,783
and they stop and sit
and stare at us.

499
00:45:34,851 --> 00:45:38,480
- What do you want to do?
- Ask the general to ask
the holy man to move.

500
00:45:38,555 --> 00:45:42,286
- It wouldn't be polite.
- I don't suppose the general
even knows he's there.

501
00:45:42,359 --> 00:45:45,795
Oh, yes he does. That old man
worries him quite a bit,

502
00:45:45,862 --> 00:45:48,387
particularly when he's
in the middle of his dinner...

503
00:45:48,465 --> 00:45:51,298
or when he's trying on
a new coat from London.

504
00:45:51,368 --> 00:45:54,929
- Why?
- I suppose he feels
he ought to do likewise.

505
00:45:55,005 --> 00:45:57,132
And he wouldn't turn him out?

506
00:45:57,207 --> 00:46:01,143
It'd be a bit awkward for the general
to turn out his own uncle.

507
00:46:01,211 --> 00:46:03,372
His uncle?

508
00:46:03,447 --> 00:46:07,076
General Sir Krishna Rai,
K CVO, K CSl, CMG.

509
00:46:07,150 --> 00:46:09,516
He has several
foreign decorations too.

510
00:46:09,586 --> 00:46:12,077
He lent our general
the money to buy this place.

511
00:46:13,723 --> 00:46:16,556
I've never heard him talk.
They say he speaks perfect English.

512
00:46:16,626 --> 00:46:18,787
Several other
European languages too.

513
00:46:23,567 --> 00:46:25,501
Does he never speak at all ?

514
00:46:25,569 --> 00:46:27,503
I've never heard him.

515
00:46:27,571 --> 00:46:29,505
When does he eat or sleep?

516
00:46:29,573 --> 00:46:32,337
No one knows. He's always
in his place under the tree.

517
00:46:32,409 --> 00:46:34,707
People come miles to see him.

518
00:46:51,094 --> 00:46:53,494
[ Sighs ]
Well, I really don't know what to do.

519
00:46:55,098 --> 00:46:58,033
What would Christ have done?

520
00:47:07,544 --> 00:47:10,274
[ Bells Jingling ]

521
00:47:22,926 --> 00:47:25,952
- Morning, General.
- Good morning, Sister Honey.

522
00:47:27,964 --> 00:47:30,432
Good morning, Sister Ruth.

523
00:47:44,948 --> 00:47:47,849
[ Quiet Chattering ]

524
00:48:11,641 --> 00:48:14,610
[ Sniffing ]

525
00:48:18,181 --> 00:48:22,117
Do you like it, Sister Ruth?
It's called Black Narcissus.

526
00:48:22,185 --> 00:48:26,349
Comes from the army/navy stores
in London.

527
00:48:26,423 --> 00:48:30,257
Black Narcissus.
I don't like scent at all.

528
00:48:30,327 --> 00:48:34,855
Oh, Sister, don't you think it's
rather common to smell of ourselves?

529
00:48:42,038 --> 00:48:45,838
-Have you seen the young general today?
- What's the latest?

530
00:48:45,909 --> 00:48:49,640
Beautiful emeralds.
The most beautiful green I've ever seen.

531
00:48:49,713 --> 00:48:51,704
At that hour of the morning,
they make me bilious.

532
00:48:51,781 --> 00:48:55,717
Have you seen his coats?
He must have a different one
for every day of the year.

533
00:48:55,785 --> 00:48:57,776
Lucky he doesn't
do his own laundry.

534
00:48:57,854 --> 00:49:01,415
Yesterday he had a coat the color
of ripe corn, patterned with flowers.

535
00:49:01,491 --> 00:49:03,721
His earrings were amethysts
three inches long,

536
00:49:03,793 --> 00:49:05,727
and his rings were turquoise.

537
00:49:05,795 --> 00:49:07,820
Today he's all jade and emeralds,

538
00:49:07,897 --> 00:49:11,628
and his coat is the most wonderful
pattern of pale violet stripes,

539
00:49:11,701 --> 00:49:14,795
just like my grandmother's
footstool.

540
00:49:25,982 --> 00:49:28,610
Oh, Granny !

541
00:49:28,685 --> 00:49:30,778
Turn around.

542
00:49:32,522 --> 00:49:36,322
These emeralds are for you,
my darling, when you marry.

543
00:49:38,228 --> 00:49:40,162
There.

544
00:49:50,774 --> 00:49:53,538
[ Whistling ]

545
00:49:53,610 --> 00:49:55,544
There's Con.

546
00:49:55,612 --> 00:49:57,910
Good night, everybody.

547
00:50:03,520 --> 00:50:05,818
Not too late, darling.

548
00:50:05,889 --> 00:50:09,222
Oh, dear, I hope they get
something settled by the winter.

549
00:50:17,300 --> 00:50:19,734
Where are you, Con?

550
00:50:19,803 --> 00:50:22,738
[ Sister Ruth ]
He said it was called Black Narcissus,

551
00:50:22,806 --> 00:50:25,070
and he got it
at the army and navy stores.

552
00:50:25,141 --> 00:50:27,609
Black Narcissus.

553
00:50:29,646 --> 00:50:31,910
That's what
I'm going to call him.

554
00:50:31,981 --> 00:50:34,347
It's a wonderful name for him.

555
00:50:34,417 --> 00:50:37,875
He's so vain, like peacock.
Fine, black peacock.

556
00:50:37,954 --> 00:50:41,321
- He's not black.
- They all look alike to me.

557
00:50:45,328 --> 00:50:48,764
General, please conjugate sasoir.

558
00:50:53,770 --> 00:50:56,637
[ Speaking French ]

559
00:51:25,802 --> 00:51:27,736
Future tense?

560
00:51:47,490 --> 00:51:51,927
[ Organ ]

561
00:51:51,995 --> 00:51:56,159
Noel, Noel

562
00:51:56,232 --> 00:52:00,168
Noel, Noel

563
00:52:00,236 --> 00:52:04,070
Born is the King

564
00:52:04,140 --> 00:52:07,109
Of Israel

565
00:52:07,177 --> 00:52:10,613
The first Noel

566
00:52:10,680 --> 00:52:14,275
-The angels did say
- [ Door Opens ]

567
00:52:14,350 --> 00:52:17,649
Was to certain poor shepherds

568
00:52:17,720 --> 00:52:21,679
In fields as they lay

569
00:52:21,758 --> 00:52:25,194
In fields as they

570
00:52:25,261 --> 00:52:28,822
[ Dean Joins In ]
Lay keeping their sheep

571
00:52:28,898 --> 00:52:32,356
On a cold winter's night

572
00:52:32,435 --> 00:52:36,531
That was so deep

573
00:52:36,606 --> 00:52:39,973
Noel, Noel

574
00:52:40,043 --> 00:52:44,207
Noel, Noel

575
00:52:44,280 --> 00:52:47,340
Born is the King

576
00:52:47,417 --> 00:52:52,320
Of Israel

577
00:52:58,261 --> 00:53:01,560
Lullay my liking

578
00:53:01,631 --> 00:53:05,533
[ Singing Continues ]

579
00:53:22,318 --> 00:53:25,287
- Something for you.
- For me?

580
00:53:25,355 --> 00:53:27,823
Christmas present.
Go on, take it.

581
00:53:27,891 --> 00:53:30,758
[ Singing Continues ]

582
00:53:32,395 --> 00:53:35,523
Oh, Con !

583
00:53:47,977 --> 00:53:50,878
[ Singing Continues ]

584
00:53:56,753 --> 00:54:00,189
[ Singing Stops ]

585
00:54:35,692 --> 00:54:38,593
Sister Clodagh.

586
00:54:40,563 --> 00:54:44,294
Sister, may I congratulate you
on the birth of Christ?

587
00:54:46,202 --> 00:54:48,136
Thank you, General.

588
00:54:48,204 --> 00:54:50,934
I hope you don't mind
my coming tonight.

589
00:54:51,007 --> 00:54:53,407
I am very much interested
in Jesus Christ.

590
00:54:56,512 --> 00:54:58,639
Have I said anything wrong?

591
00:54:58,715 --> 00:55:04,347
No, but we don't usually
speak of Him so casually.

592
00:55:04,420 --> 00:55:08,288
And you should.
He should be casual...

593
00:55:08,358 --> 00:55:11,088
[ Slurring ]
and as much a part of life
as your daily bread.

594
00:55:20,436 --> 00:55:22,597
How dare you
come here like this !

595
00:55:22,672 --> 00:55:26,199
How dare you come
to our service tonight !

596
00:55:26,275 --> 00:55:28,539
You're--
You're unforgivable !

597
00:55:28,611 --> 00:55:30,772
You're objectionable
when you're sober...

598
00:55:30,847 --> 00:55:32,974
and abominable
when you're drunk !

599
00:55:39,122 --> 00:55:41,317
I quite agree.

600
00:55:41,391 --> 00:55:44,485
If you have a spark
of decency left in you,

601
00:55:44,560 --> 00:55:47,154
you won't come near us again !

602
00:55:50,800 --> 00:55:55,999
No, I won't be a nun

603
00:55:56,072 --> 00:56:01,135
No, I cannot be a nun

604
00:56:01,210 --> 00:56:07,012
For I am so fond of pleasure

605
00:56:07,083 --> 00:56:10,575
I cannot be a nun

606
00:56:10,653 --> 00:56:13,417
[ Laughing ]

607
00:56:13,489 --> 00:56:15,719
Happy Christmas !

608
00:56:15,792 --> 00:56:18,226
I do like his voice.

609
00:56:18,294 --> 00:56:20,888
It's so nice and loud.

610
00:56:20,963 --> 00:56:23,830
I think it's lovely, don't you?

611
00:56:23,900 --> 00:56:26,061
Good night, General.

612
00:56:26,135 --> 00:56:28,467
Good night, Sister Clodagh.

613
00:56:51,327 --> 00:56:53,454
- [ KnockAt Door ]
- Come in.

614
00:57:01,871 --> 00:57:05,705
I want to talk to you.
Come and sit down.

615
00:57:09,212 --> 00:57:12,079
I've been worried about you
for some time.

616
00:57:12,148 --> 00:57:14,776
I feel that things
are not right with you.

617
00:57:14,851 --> 00:57:16,785
In what way?

618
00:57:16,853 --> 00:57:20,016
You look so ill, and
you've got so terribly thin.

619
00:57:20,089 --> 00:57:22,717
I know that you're trying
to keep up for all our sakes,

620
00:57:22,792 --> 00:57:26,091
but I feel that you must go in
with Sister Briony and see the doctor.

621
00:57:26,162 --> 00:57:29,097
I shan't see the doctor !
I'm perfectly well and right !

622
00:57:29,165 --> 00:57:32,100
You're just trying
to make out that--

623
00:57:36,405 --> 00:57:39,169
I didn't mean to be rude.

624
00:57:41,244 --> 00:57:43,269
I haven't been sleeping,
that's all.

625
00:57:45,748 --> 00:57:49,411
If you haven't been sleeping,
there must be some reason for it.

626
00:57:49,485 --> 00:57:51,680
Can't you tell me?

627
00:57:51,754 --> 00:57:54,518
Is something worrying you?

628
00:57:54,590 --> 00:57:57,753
Yes. Yes, that's it.

629
00:57:57,827 --> 00:58:00,591
I'm worried.

630
00:58:02,231 --> 00:58:05,257
Don't you think
you could tell me about it?

631
00:58:10,106 --> 00:58:12,370
I'd like you to tell me,
if you can.

632
00:58:14,277 --> 00:58:18,213
I can't speak of it... to anyone.

633
00:58:18,281 --> 00:58:21,546
Won't you try ?
You know you can trust me.

634
00:58:21,617 --> 00:58:25,519
You didn't want me to come here.
None of you have ever wanted me.

635
00:58:27,790 --> 00:58:30,884
Don't you think you're letting
things run away with you?

636
00:58:35,364 --> 00:58:39,425
I think you have let yourself fall...

637
00:58:39,502 --> 00:58:42,869
into thinking too much of Mr. Dean.

638
00:58:46,275 --> 00:58:50,075
Sister, don't you realize
what you're doing,

639
00:58:50,146 --> 00:58:53,013
what you're running the risk
of losing in yourself?

640
00:58:53,082 --> 00:58:57,712
Sister, you must-- I must make you see
before it is too late.

641
00:58:57,787 --> 00:59:01,086
All the same, I've noticed you're
very pleased to see him yourself !

642
00:59:05,294 --> 00:59:09,321
If that was in your mind, it's better
said I think you're out of your senses !

643
00:59:09,398 --> 00:59:13,164
Listen to me. I don't know--
I can't decide now what to make of you.

644
00:59:13,236 --> 00:59:17,400
I shall have to think,
and I want you to think too.

645
00:59:17,473 --> 00:59:20,067
As for Mr. Dean--

646
00:59:22,078 --> 00:59:25,775
In spite of his charm and kindliness,
he is not a good man.

647
00:59:25,848 --> 00:59:30,876
You must take him for what he is
and not try to glorify him
into something he is not.

648
00:59:30,953 --> 00:59:34,548
When he came to chapel on
Christmas night, he was drunk.

649
00:59:34,624 --> 00:59:36,558
Can I go?

650
00:59:39,695 --> 00:59:43,290
I want you to write
to Reverend Mother.

651
00:59:43,366 --> 00:59:46,961
I shan't look at the letter,
and her reply will be your own business.

652
00:59:47,036 --> 00:59:49,129
Am I to write
two or three pages?

653
00:59:49,205 --> 00:59:52,697
Would you rather I did it now,
or shall I finish my class work first?

654
00:59:56,212 --> 00:59:58,976
You may go.

655
01:00:06,222 --> 01:00:08,349
[ Door Slams ]

656
01:01:10,119 --> 01:01:12,383
That parcel is mine.
Give it to me.

657
01:01:12,455 --> 01:01:16,391
I can't, Lemani. I must give
all the mail to Sister Clodagh.

658
01:01:16,459 --> 01:01:19,724
It's mine. Give it to me, you fool.
It's addressed to me.

659
01:01:19,795 --> 01:01:22,628
Look, I ordered it myself
from Calcutta.

660
01:01:22,698 --> 01:01:25,098
It's nothing to do
with anyone else.

661
01:01:31,540 --> 01:01:35,271
Sister Briony, do you know what's
happened to the other gold chain?

662
01:01:35,344 --> 01:01:37,608
No. It was there when
we had it out at Christmas.

663
01:01:37,680 --> 01:01:40,342
- Well, it isn't here now.
- Ask Kanchi if she's seen it.

664
01:01:40,416 --> 01:01:42,350
[ Screaming ]

665
01:01:42,418 --> 01:01:45,410
And that for stealing
in my house !

666
01:01:45,488 --> 01:01:49,618
-And that for stealing a brass chain !
- [ Screaming Continues ]

667
01:01:49,692 --> 01:01:53,856
That's for stealing it
in such a silly way !

668
01:01:53,929 --> 01:01:58,229
And that is
for getting found out !

669
01:02:04,573 --> 01:02:07,906
[ Screams, Sobbing ]

670
01:02:16,685 --> 01:02:20,086
- What has the girl done?
- She's a thief !

671
01:02:20,156 --> 01:02:22,954
She stole a brass chain
from the church room...

672
01:02:23,025 --> 01:02:25,186
to put around her dirty neck !

673
01:02:25,261 --> 01:02:29,197
Finish the beating,
my little general.

674
01:02:29,265 --> 01:02:31,927
You're going to be
a great man.

675
01:02:32,001 --> 01:02:34,663
Not like your uncle.
Oh, dear, no.

676
01:02:34,737 --> 01:02:38,537
Like your grandfather !
[ Laughs ]

677
01:02:38,607 --> 01:02:40,939
He was a man !

678
01:02:41,010 --> 01:02:44,343
Finish the beating,
and begin to be a man !

679
01:02:44,413 --> 01:02:47,280
[ Laughing Continues ]

680
01:02:50,853 --> 01:02:53,822
[ Sobbing Continues ]

681
01:02:53,889 --> 01:02:55,948
Get up.

682
01:03:54,116 --> 01:03:57,882
- Forget-me-not.
- Forget-me-not.

683
01:03:57,953 --> 01:04:02,413
- Sweet pea.
- Sweet pea.

684
01:04:04,293 --> 01:04:08,127
- Daffodil.
- Daffodil.

685
01:04:09,899 --> 01:04:13,266
Japanese peony.

686
01:04:13,335 --> 01:04:16,793
Japanese peony.

687
01:04:16,872 --> 01:04:20,364
Chinese lily.

688
01:04:20,442 --> 01:04:23,138
Chinese lily.

689
01:04:23,212 --> 01:04:25,407
Tulip.

690
01:04:25,481 --> 01:04:27,574
Tulip.

691
01:04:27,650 --> 01:04:31,586
- Honeysuckle.
- Honeysuckle.

692
01:04:31,654 --> 01:04:34,782
Honeysuckle.

693
01:04:34,857 --> 01:04:38,088
Delphinium.

694
01:04:38,160 --> 01:04:41,527
- Sister Honey !
- Delphinium.

695
01:04:41,597 --> 01:04:44,964
Will you find Sister Philippa
for me, please?

696
01:04:46,235 --> 01:04:48,567
- And the cabbage patch?
- Fox gloves.

697
01:04:48,637 --> 01:04:51,902
- And the runner beans?
- Honeysuckle.

698
01:04:51,974 --> 01:04:55,137
- And the onions?
- Tulips.

699
01:04:55,211 --> 01:04:58,874
And the potatoes?
All flowers?

700
01:05:01,817 --> 01:05:05,344
No, not the little round bed.
And there's more vegetables...

701
01:05:05,421 --> 01:05:07,855
down by the stables
where they won't show.

702
01:05:07,923 --> 01:05:10,118
But what on earth
came over you--

703
01:05:14,196 --> 01:05:16,926
Would you like to sit down?

704
01:05:18,234 --> 01:05:21,067
Sister, I want
to be transferred.

705
01:05:22,538 --> 01:05:24,472
Transferred?

706
01:05:24,540 --> 01:05:27,976
Yes, I want you to write
and ask for my transfer at once.

707
01:05:30,012 --> 01:05:32,276
If you will, at once.

708
01:05:33,916 --> 01:05:35,850
But why?

709
01:05:35,918 --> 01:05:38,648
I was becoming
too fond of the place.

710
01:05:38,721 --> 01:05:42,487
I was too wrapped up
in my work. l--

711
01:05:42,558 --> 01:05:45,152
I thought too much about it.

712
01:05:45,227 --> 01:05:47,661
I'd forgotten--

713
01:05:47,730 --> 01:05:50,927
Forgotten what?

714
01:05:51,000 --> 01:05:52,934
What I am.

715
01:05:53,002 --> 01:05:55,903
I was losing the spirit
of our order.

716
01:05:55,971 --> 01:05:58,838
I've been thinking
it over, you see,

717
01:05:58,907 --> 01:06:01,637
and I must go at once.

718
01:06:05,247 --> 01:06:08,683
I don't see that at all.

719
01:06:08,751 --> 01:06:11,584
Now that you know
and you realize the danger,

720
01:06:11,654 --> 01:06:13,588
you needn't go.

721
01:06:13,656 --> 01:06:16,284
Surely now is the time to stay.

722
01:06:16,358 --> 01:06:18,292
I daren't stay.

723
01:06:18,360 --> 01:06:21,921
I think there are only two ways
of living in this place.

724
01:06:21,997 --> 01:06:26,093
Either you must live
like Mr. Dean, or--

725
01:06:26,168 --> 01:06:29,035
or like the holy man.

726
01:06:29,104 --> 01:06:32,665
Either ignore it,
or give yourself up to it.

727
01:06:34,943 --> 01:06:37,207
Neither would do for us.

728
01:06:37,279 --> 01:06:40,043
No.

729
01:06:40,115 --> 01:06:44,882
Well, we are here, and I don't think
it will help matters if we run away.

730
01:06:51,794 --> 01:06:55,457
You know if I ask
for you to be transferred,
it'll be a bad mark against you?

731
01:06:55,531 --> 01:07:00,332
That's all the better.
That's what I need.

732
01:07:02,638 --> 01:07:05,698
Ayah ! Ayah !

733
01:07:22,157 --> 01:07:25,092
- [ Speaking Hindi ]
- What did she say?

734
01:07:25,160 --> 01:07:27,685
[ Speaking Hindi ]

735
01:07:27,763 --> 01:07:30,698
It's Alma's little brother.

736
01:07:30,766 --> 01:07:33,166
Shall we give him magnesia?

737
01:07:33,235 --> 01:07:36,329
Or some of the paraffinic mulch?

738
01:07:44,413 --> 01:07:47,280
[ Gasps ]
A hundred and three !

739
01:07:47,349 --> 01:07:51,342
That's not much in a baby.
They go up and down easily, don't they ?

740
01:07:51,420 --> 01:07:54,821
[ Speaking Hindi ]

741
01:07:54,890 --> 01:07:56,824
It's been three days.

742
01:07:56,892 --> 01:07:59,827
This morning he wouldn't
wake, so she brought him.

743
01:07:59,895 --> 01:08:04,093
Let him sleep. Take him home,
and put him on your bed.

744
01:08:04,166 --> 01:08:07,533
[ Speaking Hindi ]

745
01:08:10,205 --> 01:08:12,469
Aren't you going
to give him anything?

746
01:08:12,541 --> 01:08:14,941
There's nothing I can do.

747
01:08:15,010 --> 01:08:18,104
But there must be
something we can do.

748
01:08:18,180 --> 01:08:22,879
At least bathe his eyes
or relieve his tummy with a little oil.

749
01:08:22,951 --> 01:08:26,580
I daren't touch him, Sister.
I don't think he feels pain.

750
01:08:26,655 --> 01:08:29,647
You've only got to look at him
to see how it must hurt him !

751
01:08:29,725 --> 01:08:32,751
You're thinking
of what Mr. Dean said !

752
01:08:32,828 --> 01:08:34,955
That's enough, Sister !

753
01:08:35,030 --> 01:08:37,726
I won't have any hysteria.
I know what I'm doing.

754
01:08:39,802 --> 01:08:43,670
The kindest thing you can do
is to make her go home,
where she'll be amongst her own people.

755
01:08:47,576 --> 01:08:49,601
[ Speaking Hindi ]

756
01:09:05,594 --> 01:09:07,619
Sister Ruth.

757
01:09:09,264 --> 01:09:11,824
Everyone's
very late this morning.

758
01:09:11,900 --> 01:09:14,528
I do hope nothing's happened.

759
01:09:17,005 --> 01:09:20,372
Joseph, go down the path
and hurry them up.

760
01:09:22,544 --> 01:09:25,479
- Well, go on.
- I don't want to.

761
01:09:25,547 --> 01:09:28,983
- You don't want to?
- Why don't you want to?

762
01:09:29,051 --> 01:09:31,952
How dare you answer me like that.
Go at once !

763
01:09:32,020 --> 01:09:34,750
- No, I won't go.
-Joseph !

764
01:09:34,823 --> 01:09:37,257
- [ Crying ]
- Now stand still.

765
01:09:37,326 --> 01:09:40,022
- Tell me what's the matter.
- Don't frighten him.

766
01:09:40,095 --> 01:09:43,496
- Why haven't the children come?
- Where are they ?

767
01:09:43,565 --> 01:09:45,726
He knows why.
Tell us.

768
01:09:45,801 --> 01:09:48,497
I don't want to.
Lemani, don't make me tell !

769
01:09:48,570 --> 01:09:51,232
Joseph, you must tell us.
Please, Joseph, dear.

770
01:09:51,306 --> 01:09:54,366
- Tell us.
- The little baby is dead !

771
01:09:54,443 --> 01:09:57,207
- Oh, no !
- Our little brother is dead !

772
01:09:57,279 --> 01:10:00,248
And they said that this man
and lemani killed him.

773
01:10:00,315 --> 01:10:02,010
- [ Gasps ]
- Sister Clodagh !

774
01:10:02,084 --> 01:10:04,245
- There's nobody in the dispensary.
- None of the children have come.

775
01:10:04,319 --> 01:10:06,344
- No gardeners.
- Kanchi has gone.

776
01:10:06,421 --> 01:10:08,719
- So has the young general.
- There isn't a servant in the place.

777
01:10:08,790 --> 01:10:11,156
We're all alone.
There's no one in the house.

778
01:10:11,226 --> 01:10:14,161
It was my fault.

779
01:10:14,229 --> 01:10:17,096
Because I loved him.
I couldn't bare to see him die.

780
01:10:17,165 --> 01:10:20,532
I did it !
I killed him !

781
01:10:20,602 --> 01:10:24,561
I gave her a bottle to take, some of our
cotton wool and one of our spoons.

782
01:10:24,640 --> 01:10:27,871
- I killed him !
- Ayah !

783
01:10:27,943 --> 01:10:30,639
Ayah, how much
of this is true?

784
01:10:30,712 --> 01:10:33,442
All true, Lemani.
The people are very angry.

785
01:10:33,515 --> 01:10:37,178
We must explain. Somebody must tell
them. We must find the young general.

786
01:10:37,252 --> 01:10:41,120
- No, he's run away with Kanchi.
- Will you take a message?

787
01:10:41,189 --> 01:10:44,818
- Me? No.
- Well, can Joseph?

788
01:10:44,893 --> 01:10:47,453
- They won't let him come back.
- I'll go.

789
01:10:47,529 --> 01:10:50,965
It's not safe for any of you
to go outside the garden.

790
01:10:51,033 --> 01:10:54,400
- You can't go, Sister.
It's far too dangerous.
- I'm not going down.

791
01:10:54,469 --> 01:10:57,131
[ Bell Clanging ]

792
01:11:24,900 --> 01:11:26,834
Tova !

793
01:11:28,737 --> 01:11:31,001
Tova, my pony, quickly.

794
01:11:35,077 --> 01:11:38,171
- Well, who was it?
- [ Blows Nose ]

795
01:11:38,246 --> 01:11:40,339
You.

796
01:11:43,752 --> 01:11:47,848
Mr. Dean, do you think it's serious?
Do you think they'll come back?

797
01:11:47,923 --> 01:11:50,517
Sister Clodagh,
the agent before my time...

798
01:11:50,592 --> 01:11:53,527
was riding down to the factory
one day on his pony.

799
01:11:53,595 --> 01:11:56,758
He let it kick an umbrella
lying open in the path.

800
01:11:56,832 --> 01:12:00,131
There was a child asleep
under it, and it was killed.

801
01:12:00,202 --> 01:12:04,969
It was just an accident,
but they murdered him that night.

802
01:12:05,040 --> 01:12:09,602
I'm not trying to frighten you, but I
want you to see that it may be serious.

803
01:12:09,678 --> 01:12:12,545
I've been down to the village.
Everything seems quiet enough.

804
01:12:12,614 --> 01:12:17,551
- Did they say anything?
- Nothing. They listened
to me and said nothing.

805
01:12:17,619 --> 01:12:21,783
I saw the woman I drank the stuff
that Sister Honey gave her.

806
01:12:21,857 --> 01:12:26,157
- You drank it?
- I wanted to prove to them
that I wouldn't drop down dead.

807
01:12:26,228 --> 01:12:28,822
It was only castor oil.

808
01:12:28,897 --> 01:12:31,229
None of you must go
out of the garden.

809
01:12:31,299 --> 01:12:33,893
Try to behave as though
nothing had happened.

810
01:12:33,969 --> 01:12:36,904
I'll go down now
and come back this evening.

811
01:13:06,068 --> 01:13:08,002
Lemani?

812
01:13:16,678 --> 01:13:18,612
Lemani?

813
01:13:23,151 --> 01:13:25,779
Lemani?

814
01:13:25,854 --> 01:13:29,051
- What's that for ?
- For you, Lemani.

815
01:13:29,124 --> 01:13:32,821
Who sent it?
Sister Clodagh?

816
01:15:01,016 --> 01:15:03,849
[ Horns Blowing ]

817
01:15:14,362 --> 01:15:17,559
Do you notice a change in us
since we came here?

818
01:15:17,632 --> 01:15:20,294
I notice a change in you.

819
01:15:20,368 --> 01:15:23,235
Am I very different?

820
01:15:23,305 --> 01:15:25,239
Yes.

821
01:15:27,242 --> 01:15:29,176
You're much nicer.

822
01:15:29,244 --> 01:15:32,441
- Nicer ?
- Mmm. You're human.

823
01:15:32,514 --> 01:15:34,448
Human?

824
01:15:35,784 --> 01:15:38,514
Yes, we're all human,
aren't we?

825
01:15:42,490 --> 01:15:45,482
When I was a girl,
I loved a man.

826
01:15:45,560 --> 01:15:48,927
We were children together
in Ireland, where I come from.

827
01:15:48,997 --> 01:15:51,932
A little place
called Dennis Kelly.

828
01:15:52,000 --> 01:15:55,436
I thought--
everyone thought--

829
01:15:55,503 --> 01:15:57,664
we should marry.

830
01:15:57,739 --> 01:16:00,003
But he was ambitious,

831
01:16:00,075 --> 01:16:03,738
and I found out he was going
to America to his uncle...

832
01:16:03,812 --> 01:16:07,009
and he didn't
intend to take me.

833
01:16:08,984 --> 01:16:11,748
He didn't think he was
doing anything wrong.

834
01:16:11,820 --> 01:16:14,789
I don't think he ever
thought of us marrying.

835
01:16:14,856 --> 01:16:17,723
But in a little
place like that,

836
01:16:17,792 --> 01:16:20,784
and I had shown I loved him,

837
01:16:20,862 --> 01:16:23,524
I had to get away first.

838
01:16:26,001 --> 01:16:28,299
And that's why
you entered the order ?

839
01:16:30,038 --> 01:16:33,132
And being you,
you wouldn't go back?

840
01:16:33,208 --> 01:16:36,700
It was a strange way
of bringing me in,

841
01:16:36,778 --> 01:16:39,303
but God works in strange ways.

842
01:16:40,548 --> 01:16:43,813
I had work to do,
and I had the life.

843
01:16:43,885 --> 01:16:47,013
No one outside can possibly know
what that means.

844
01:16:47,088 --> 01:16:49,352
It came to be my life.

845
01:16:49,424 --> 01:16:52,655
I had forgotten everything
until I came here.

846
01:16:56,665 --> 01:16:59,133
The first day I came,
I thought of him...

847
01:16:59,200 --> 01:17:01,760
for the first time for years.

848
01:17:01,836 --> 01:17:06,398
I seem to go back to the first time
I loved him, when we were children.

849
01:17:08,276 --> 01:17:12,212
The young general
reminds me of him too.

850
01:17:12,280 --> 01:17:15,716
The world comes
thrusting in behind him.

851
01:17:17,018 --> 01:17:20,010
I've been drifting and dreaming,

852
01:17:20,088 --> 01:17:24,787
and now I seem to be living through
the struggle and the bitterness again.

853
01:17:30,432 --> 01:17:34,129
Here. It's quite clean.
I washed my hair this morning.

854
01:17:37,772 --> 01:17:41,208
-[ Sighs ]
-Don't take on so. There's a good girl.

855
01:17:41,276 --> 01:17:44,712
It'll all blow over.
There's nothing really wrong.

856
01:17:44,779 --> 01:17:47,373
Sister Philippa is leaving,

857
01:17:47,449 --> 01:17:50,885
and this morning I had a letter
from Reverend Mother.

858
01:17:50,952 --> 01:17:53,284
Sister Ruth
is giving up the order.

859
01:17:53,355 --> 01:17:55,880
She has not renewed her vows.

860
01:17:55,957 --> 01:17:58,118
I'm sorry.

861
01:17:58,193 --> 01:18:01,594
And you--
Ever since we came here,

862
01:18:01,663 --> 01:18:04,257
over all our troubles,
it's been,

863
01:18:04,332 --> 01:18:07,301
"Ask Mr. Dean. Ask Mr. Dean."

864
01:18:07,369 --> 01:18:09,997
There was just no one else
you could ask.

865
01:18:12,040 --> 01:18:14,702
But I had to take the young general.

866
01:18:14,776 --> 01:18:17,540
I couldn't turn out the holy man.

867
01:18:17,612 --> 01:18:20,046
I couldn't stop
the wind from blowing...

868
01:18:20,115 --> 01:18:22,982
and the air from being
as clear as crystal...

869
01:18:23,051 --> 01:18:25,246
and I couldn't hide the mountain.

870
01:18:25,320 --> 01:18:28,551
Look, you must get away from here,
all of you, at once.

871
01:18:30,492 --> 01:18:33,256
- Run away?
- Yes, if you've got any sense.

872
01:18:33,328 --> 01:18:36,024
What, leave all this work,
like the brothers?

873
01:18:36,097 --> 01:18:37,758
Yes.

874
01:18:39,401 --> 01:18:42,598
I told you it was no place
to put a nunnery.

875
01:18:42,670 --> 01:18:47,073
There's something in the atmosphere
that makes everything seem exaggerated.

876
01:18:47,142 --> 01:18:50,703
Don't you understand? You must
all get away before something happens !

877
01:19:19,641 --> 01:19:22,508
[ Drums Continue ]

878
01:19:49,604 --> 01:19:52,664
[ Quiet Praying ]

879
01:19:52,740 --> 01:19:55,766
And drive from it
all snares of the enemy.

880
01:19:55,844 --> 01:19:59,905
May Thy holy angels dwell here
and keep us in peace.

881
01:19:59,981 --> 01:20:03,348
May Thy blessing be--
[ Continues, Indistinct ]

882
01:20:03,418 --> 01:20:06,353
[ Sobbing ]

883
01:20:15,663 --> 01:20:18,097
[ Snoring ]

884
01:20:32,280 --> 01:20:34,544
Sister, are you there?

885
01:20:41,055 --> 01:20:43,489
[ Knocking ]

886
01:20:47,295 --> 01:20:50,389
Sister, do you want me
to wake the others?

887
01:20:57,238 --> 01:21:01,174
You can't order me about.
You have nothing to do with me anymore.

888
01:21:01,242 --> 01:21:04,473
I know what you've done.
I know that you've left the order.

889
01:21:04,546 --> 01:21:08,073
I only want to stop you from doing
something you'll be sorry for.

890
01:21:08,149 --> 01:21:11,414
Sister Philippa
is going back in a few days.
I want to send you with her.

891
01:21:11,486 --> 01:21:15,183
That's what you would like to do,
send me back and shut me up.

892
01:21:15,256 --> 01:21:18,225
That's what you would all
like to do !

893
01:21:41,015 --> 01:21:43,347
You know that isn't true.

894
01:21:43,418 --> 01:21:46,080
Why should we want to keep you
here against your will ?

895
01:21:46,154 --> 01:21:49,715
Because you're all
jealous of me, especially you !

896
01:21:54,195 --> 01:21:56,823
At least wait till the morning.

897
01:21:58,733 --> 01:22:01,668
Wait till the morning,
and I'll wait with you.

898
01:22:06,908 --> 01:22:09,934
[ Snickers ]

899
01:24:02,990 --> 01:24:05,618
[ Pounding On Door ]

900
01:24:05,693 --> 01:24:08,184
[ Laughing ]

901
01:24:16,070 --> 01:24:19,301
- Ayah, wake up !
- Oh, what is it? What is it?

902
01:24:19,374 --> 01:24:22,400
It's Sister Ruth !
Stop her ! She's gone mad !

903
01:24:22,477 --> 01:24:25,776
- [ Screams ] Oh, it's my fault !
- Shhh !

904
01:24:27,849 --> 01:24:30,943
Can't stop her.
I think we should leave them alone.

905
01:24:31,018 --> 01:24:33,680
-She may kill herself.
-lf she's really mad, that won't happen.

906
01:24:33,755 --> 01:24:36,918
Quick, search the house !
We must stop her ! Sister Ruth.

907
01:24:36,991 --> 01:24:39,255
Sister Ruth !
Sister Ruth !

908
01:24:39,327 --> 01:24:41,591
We must get Lanchi.

909
01:24:41,662 --> 01:24:43,630
Sister Ruth !

910
01:24:46,300 --> 01:24:48,996
Sister Ruth !
Sister Ruth !

911
01:24:49,070 --> 01:24:51,197
- Sister Ruth !
- Sister Ruth !

912
01:24:51,272 --> 01:24:53,331
- Sister Ruth !
- Sister Ruth !

913
01:24:53,408 --> 01:24:55,342
Sister Ruth !

914
01:25:04,852 --> 01:25:07,616
[ Sister Clodagh ]
Joseph, ask him if he's seen her !

915
01:25:07,688 --> 01:25:10,589
Oh, no, Lemani,
we couldn't do that.

916
01:25:10,658 --> 01:25:13,923
But, Joseph, anything
may have happened to the lemani.
She may be hurt.

917
01:25:13,995 --> 01:25:17,431
That would be a very little
thing to him, Lemani.

918
01:25:17,498 --> 01:25:19,659
He wouldn't notice it.

919
01:25:19,734 --> 01:25:22,669
[ Drums Continue ]

920
01:25:30,411 --> 01:25:33,710
- [ Animal Roars ]
- [ Gasps ]

921
01:25:33,781 --> 01:25:36,716
[ Birds Squawking ]

922
01:26:21,662 --> 01:26:24,256
[ Bird Whistling ]

923
01:26:54,028 --> 01:26:56,087
Good evening.

924
01:27:01,402 --> 01:27:03,336
Sister Ruth?

925
01:27:04,672 --> 01:27:07,732
I can't stand it any longer.
I left the order.

926
01:27:07,808 --> 01:27:11,005
I gave up my vows.
I've finished with them up there.

927
01:27:11,078 --> 01:27:13,012
I see.

928
01:27:14,649 --> 01:27:17,482
I can arrange for you
to stay at the rest house.

929
01:27:17,552 --> 01:27:19,679
I'll send my boy over now.

930
01:27:19,754 --> 01:27:23,155
In the morning, I'll get ponies
and porters to take you to Darjeeling.

931
01:27:25,159 --> 01:27:27,992
- I love you.
- You--

932
01:27:28,062 --> 01:27:31,395
Well, if you do,
you can forget about it.

933
01:27:31,465 --> 01:27:33,456
[ Cries ]

934
01:27:36,037 --> 01:27:38,471
I'm sorry, Sister Ruth.
Very sorry, but--

935
01:27:38,539 --> 01:27:41,337
Look, let me take you
back to the palace.

936
01:27:41,409 --> 01:27:44,936
It isn't too late. Sister Clodagh
is your friend. She wants to help you.

937
01:27:45,012 --> 01:27:47,708
She hates me.
They all hate me.

938
01:27:47,782 --> 01:27:51,240
- You're the only one
that's ever been kind to me.
- I've hardly spoken to you.

939
01:27:51,319 --> 01:27:54,914
Yes, you have. When I stopped
the old woman from bleeding to death,

940
01:27:54,989 --> 01:27:57,583
- you said you were grateful.
- Did I ?

941
01:27:57,658 --> 01:28:00,092
And then when you stopped me
that day in the hall--

942
01:28:00,161 --> 01:28:03,995
Oh, whatever I said, it didn't
mean a thing ! You've all gone crazy.

943
01:28:04,065 --> 01:28:07,466
Well, drive one another crazy,
but leave me out of it !

944
01:28:07,535 --> 01:28:10,868
- Are you going to Darjeeling or not?
- No !

945
01:28:10,938 --> 01:28:13,805
- Then you must go back to the palace.
- No.

946
01:28:13,874 --> 01:28:16,775
You'll go back
if I have to carry you back.

947
01:28:16,844 --> 01:28:20,177
Go and talk to Sister Clodagh. She
brought you here. She can get you back.

948
01:28:20,247 --> 01:28:22,340
Sister Clodagh !
Sister Clodagh !

949
01:28:22,416 --> 01:28:24,782
- Do you know what she says about you?
- Whatever she said, it was true !

950
01:28:24,852 --> 01:28:28,083
- You love her !
- I don't love anyone !

951
01:28:28,155 --> 01:28:32,922
Clodagh ! Clodagh !
Clodagh ! Clodagh !

952
01:28:32,994 --> 01:28:36,293
Clodagh ! Clodagh !
[ Crashes ]

953
01:28:52,313 --> 01:28:54,338
Feel better now?

954
01:29:03,124 --> 01:29:06,753
All right, I'll go.

955
01:29:06,827 --> 01:29:11,389
That's a good girl.
Try and get some sleep.

956
01:29:11,465 --> 01:29:13,558
In the morning you'll wake up...

957
01:29:13,634 --> 01:29:15,898
and be sorry you made
such a fool of yourself.

958
01:29:15,970 --> 01:29:19,235
- Come on, I'll come with you.
- I'll go alone.

959
01:29:19,306 --> 01:29:23,675
- You'll do nothing of the sort.
- I'll go alone or not at all.

960
01:29:27,014 --> 01:29:28,948
Suit yourself.

961
01:30:04,351 --> 01:30:07,479
- [ Gasps ]
- It's morning, Lemani.

962
01:30:07,555 --> 01:30:12,254
Oh, yes, Joseph, it's morning.
What time is it?

963
01:30:12,326 --> 01:30:15,523
5:45 by Auntie's watch.

964
01:30:19,166 --> 01:30:21,634
Fine day, Lemani.

965
01:30:21,702 --> 01:30:25,695
People call it
the flowing of the snows.

966
01:30:27,174 --> 01:30:30,803
Joseph, if Sister Briony asks
for me, I'll be in the chapel.

967
01:31:49,089 --> 01:31:52,024
[ Door Opens ]

968
01:34:01,989 --> 01:34:05,686
[ Bell Clanging ]

969
01:34:10,130 --> 01:34:12,496
Hail Mary, full of grace,

970
01:34:12,566 --> 01:34:14,625
blessed is the fruit
of thy womb.

971
01:34:14,702 --> 01:34:17,136
[ Bell Continues ]

972
01:34:36,757 --> 01:34:39,487
[ Screaming ]

973
01:34:45,899 --> 01:34:48,493
[ Gasps ]

974
01:34:49,770 --> 01:34:51,704
[ Screams ]

975
01:34:57,444 --> 01:35:00,607
[ Screaming ]

976
01:35:05,519 --> 01:35:08,249
[ Drums Continue ]

977
01:35:11,058 --> 01:35:13,288
[ Drums Stop ]

978
01:35:21,335 --> 01:35:24,270
[ Chattering ]

979
01:35:58,705 --> 01:36:01,640
What do you want, General ?

980
01:36:10,384 --> 01:36:13,945
Sister, you know
I have not been here lately,

981
01:36:14,021 --> 01:36:16,922
and I'm deeply sorry
about Sister Ruth.

982
01:36:16,990 --> 01:36:21,017
Thank you.
Is there anything else?

983
01:36:21,095 --> 01:36:25,054
You're cross with me.
Please do not be cross with me.

984
01:36:25,132 --> 01:36:28,659
I've done a very wrong thing,
but I didn't mean to do it.

985
01:36:28,735 --> 01:36:31,761
Isn't it rather late
to tell me about that?

986
01:36:31,839 --> 01:36:35,275
Yes. Yes, it is, rather.

987
01:36:35,342 --> 01:36:38,675
I don't mean to do
anything wrong again.

988
01:36:38,745 --> 01:36:41,680
I'm going to give up
being clever and famous.

989
01:36:41,748 --> 01:36:44,512
I'm going to be
exactly like my ancestors.

990
01:36:44,585 --> 01:36:46,985
They were warriors and princes.

991
01:36:47,054 --> 01:36:49,454
They were modest
and brave and polite,

992
01:36:49,523 --> 01:36:52,151
and they never did
anything cheating.

993
01:36:52,226 --> 01:36:55,957
That is why I came to you
as soon as I thought of it...

994
01:36:56,029 --> 01:36:58,623
to tell you what I have done.

995
01:36:58,699 --> 01:37:01,167
Must you tell me now?

996
01:37:01,235 --> 01:37:04,033
- Please, Sister.
- Well, what have you done?

997
01:37:08,909 --> 01:37:14,176
Sister Clodagh, I didn't know how
to tell you, so I asked Mr. Dean.

998
01:37:14,248 --> 01:37:19,049
He said to tell it was
the story of the prince...

999
01:37:19,119 --> 01:37:21,280
and the beggar maid.

1000
01:37:23,323 --> 01:37:26,121
[ Chattering Continues ]

1001
01:38:07,734 --> 01:38:09,759
[ Speaks Hindi ]

1002
01:38:17,844 --> 01:38:20,608
You said you'd give us
till the rains break.

1003
01:38:20,681 --> 01:38:23,206
They haven't broken yet.

1004
01:38:23,283 --> 01:38:26,116
What will they do
with you down there?

1005
01:38:26,186 --> 01:38:29,815
I shall be sent to another convent
with less responsibility.

1006
01:38:29,890 --> 01:38:33,326
I shall be superseded
as sister-in-charge.

1007
01:38:33,393 --> 01:38:35,588
Will you be able to stomach that?

1008
01:38:35,662 --> 01:38:38,597
Stiff-necked, obstinate
creature like you?

1009
01:38:38,665 --> 01:38:40,963
It's what I need.

1010
01:38:41,034 --> 01:38:45,130
I expect I shall have to remind
myself of it a hundred times a day.

1011
01:38:45,205 --> 01:38:48,800
I can't change in a minute
like the young general.

1012
01:38:50,210 --> 01:38:53,202
But I shall have my ghosts
to remind me.

1013
01:38:53,280 --> 01:38:56,249
You're leaving me
with more than one.

1014
01:38:58,852 --> 01:39:01,753
Will you do
one last thing for me?

1015
01:39:01,822 --> 01:39:04,347
I know you'd rather not do it.

1016
01:39:04,424 --> 01:39:06,483
Of course I'll do it.

1017
01:39:06,560 --> 01:39:09,552
Will you
look after the grave?

1018
01:39:09,630 --> 01:39:11,564
All right.

1019
01:39:15,235 --> 01:39:17,169
Good-bye.

1020
01:39:25,078 --> 01:39:27,012
Good-bye.

1021
01:39:32,953 --> 01:39:35,854
[ Chattering Continues ]
